# Generated by provisioning and deployment scripts
.env
.env-local
.hosts
.hosts-local
data/
ansible/host_vars/

# Alpha stand-up artefacts. Generated by the provisioners and
# build-inventory.sh; they carry node IPs and deployment addresses, and are
# regenerated rather than reviewed. The testnet-0 equivalents (.hosts,
# ansible/inventory.yml) were already ignored — these are their counterparts.
.hosts-alpha
.clouds-alpha
.env-alpha
ansible/inventory-alpha.yml

# Perf harness output from alpha runs. Raw per-operation records — roughly 90k
# lines and 9 MB per run, one line per keygen/sign, regenerated every time.
#
# Note this is the SAME format as perf-baseline.jsonl and perf-local.jsonl,
# which ARE tracked on purpose as reference data. The difference is intent, not
# size or shape: those are two curated baselines, whereas these accumulate one
# file per experiment (per log level, per committee, per wipe) and a reflexive
# `git add .` after an afternoon of runs commits tens of megabytes nobody will
# read again.
#
# To keep a run as a new reference point, force-add that one file:
#   git add -f testnet/perf-alpha-<description>.jsonl
perf-alpha*.jsonl
